# Growth mandate (Idle Party)

**Locked 2026-09-12.** Source: `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md` (research-checked).
Numbered programs / “next plan” removed **2026-09-14** by owner.
Play numbers: `docs/PLAY_GROWTH.md`. Why: `docs/LEARNINGS.md`.

**Default:** owner names the work. Vague “gör bättre / vad härnäst” → ask
once; do not invent a numbered program; do not restore AL20 as the batch.
AL20 play notes are a **quality gate**, not the batch.
Endgame / GEAR follow-up only when play notes say they lie.

## Do this

- Play-install first hour still holds (combat ≤90 s; hide GOLD/SHOP/ESSENCE)
- TODAY grow-the-party until the first boss; one cave today on day 2–7
- Week-1 crawl identity only against play notes (packs / tells, not dungeon #16)
- Cadence 2–3 weeks; new-player What’s New; DPS HIGH still fails CI
- Listing experiment deferred until traffic exists. No scaled UA while D1 unread

## Do not do

- New zone / class / God Hand redesign / second sim / gacha / iOS / web product
- AL20 chase/wipe polish as the default slice
- God-object cleanup as the quarter’s story
- Scaled paid UA (tiny spend ≠ a D1 study; D1 still not a readable %)
- Invent “Program N” roadmaps unless the owner asks

## Decision policy

`.cursor/rules/studio-seats.mdc` — six chairs, not a persona play.
EP + UX + Marketing pick *what to build* when the owner names a goal.
Game Director vetoes a broken fight. Tech vetoes red analyze / crash.
Legal/fairness sit on Art + Game + EP.
